Dullahan Titans appeared in Irish mythology as fearsome fairies with a role similar to the grim reaper. They would either ride in a chariot driven by six black, headless horses or on top of a lone black horse. Their shields, bearing the visage of a face, were interpreted to be the Dullahans' heads. They became omens of death said to guide dying souls to their final resting places. {{source|wikipedia:Dullahan|Wikipedia}}

Numerous Dullahan and [[Firbolg]] Titans stood as guardians of [[Tír na nÓg]] where they attacked [[Scarlet Byrne]], [[Den Fears]], [[Sophie Casterwill]] and [[Dante Vale]], and fought against [[Sabriel|Powerbonded Sabriel]] and [[Kaioh the Tracker]]. Despire overpowering the team, Dullahan was defeated when [[Lok Lambert]] returned from the [[Inter-dimensional World]] and invoked [[Pendragon]], the Legendary Titan of Champions. His Amulet was then obtained by Den. {{source|Back Home}}

Den invoked Dullahan in the tomb of [[Nostradamus]] alongside Dante's [[Elf King Oberon]] where they fought against [[Marduk]]'s [[Psikofen]] and [[Helinx]] Titans. {{source|Words from Eathon}}

In the final battle against [[The Betrayer]], Dullahan was invoked alongside [[Harrison Fears]]'s [[Jericho]]. He was defeated however by [[Demigorgan]], the Titan of Betrayal. {{source|Dante's Return}}
